<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>Grouped and ungrouped tables: Nunjucks examples and options</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="./assets/css/main.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="./preview.css">
</head>
<body class="design-system-preview">
    <main class="ons-container ons-container--wide preview-layout">
        <h1>Tables: Nunjucks examples and options</h1>
        <p>Meeting prototype using @ons/design-system {{ designSystemVersion }}. One Table component, two structures, with shared macro options.</p>
        <p>These are working calls to the existing <code>onsTable</code> macro, not a new API for the JavaScript data visualisation tables. All values are illustrative.</p>
        <p><a href="./">Back to the data visualisation context preview</a></p>
        <nav aria-label="Table examples" class="preview-choices">
            {% for example in examples %}
                <a href="#{{ example.key }}">{{ example.title }}</a>
            {% endfor %}
        </nav>
        {% for example in examples %}
            <section id="{{ example.key }}" aria-labelledby="{{ example.key }}-heading">
                <h2 id="{{ example.key }}-heading">{{ example.title }}</h2>
                <p>{{ example.description }}</p>
                {% if example.key == "grouped" %}
                    <p><strong>Prototype limitation:</strong> this demonstrates the native macro's merged cells, not the publication template's full grouped-header semantics. The native macro uses <code>scope="row"</code> for row headings, including merged headings. Group associations need dedicated accessibility review before production use.</p>
                {% endif %}
                {{ example.html | safe }}
                <details class="preview-documentation">
                    <summary>Nunjucks for {{ example.title | lower }}</summary>
                    <pre class="preview-code"><code>{{ example.source }}</code></pre>
                </details>
                <details class="preview-documentation" open>
                    <summary>Nunjucks macro options for {{ example.title | lower }}</summary>
                    <p>Options used by these two examples only. Both use the same native macro and options; grouping is expressed through cells and <code>rowspan</code>, not a <code>grouped</code> parameter.</p>
                    <div class="preview-options" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Macro options for {{ example.title | lower }}">
                        {{ macroOptions | safe }}
                    </div>
                </details>
                <details class="preview-documentation">
                    <summary>HTML for {{ example.title | lower }}</summary>
                    <pre class="preview-code"><code>{{ example.html }}</code></pre>
                </details>
            </section>
        {% endfor %}
    </main>
</body>
</html>
